{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-assembly-projector-exists","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:assembly-projector-exists","kind":"proposition","title":"Existence of the symmetric-block assembly projector","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-molecular-assembly-projector"],"cites":["references/wenzl1988","references/kassel1995"],"tags":["assembly-projector","existence","idempotent","q-young-symmetrizer","delocalization"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Molecular.symmetric_assembly_projector_exists","text":"assembly-projector-exists.md","leanSource":"assembly-projector-exists.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:assembly-projector-exists\"></a><p><em>For every strand-partition <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda</code> of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N</code> there exists a symmetric-block assembly projector <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e_{\\lambda,(N)} \\in H_N(q)</code>, and it is idempotent for generic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>.</em></p>\n<p>This is the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformation of the classical Young symmetriser.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/assembly-projector-exists.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"18.2.4","page":"b/prop-assembly-projector-exists","qa":{"counts":{"pass":92,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":5},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Molecular.symmetric_assembly_projector_exists","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/assembly-projector-exists.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
